Good, the edits succeeded. Now let me also fix the `toggleAllCheckbox` handler in the same way. Currently it sets `cb.checked = completed` which is a similar issue - setting checked on all checkboxes programmatically could cause the same detachment problem when toggle-all is used.

Actually, wait. The toggle-all test might be failing too. But the reported errors are specifically about marking/unmarking individual items. Let me still fix toggle-all for consistency, since the same issue could occur.

Actually, looking at the toggle-all code more carefully:

```javascript
toggleAllCheckbox.addEventListener('click', function () {
    ...
    var items = todoList.querySelectorAll('li');
    items.forEach(function (li) {
      if (completed) {
        li.classList.add('completed');
      } else {
        li.classList.remove('completed');
      }
      var cb = li.querySelector('.toggle');
      if (cb) cb.checked = completed;
    });
    refreshControls();
  });
```

For toggle-all, clicking the #toggle-all checkbox toggles ALL items. The individual todo checkboxes were NOT clicked by the user, so their checked state hasn't been changed by the browser natively. We DO need to set them programmatically here because the user only clicked the toggle-all checkbox, not the individual todo checkboxes.

So the toggle-all case is different - only the toggle-all checkbox itself was clicked by the user. The individual toggle checkboxes NEED their checked state set programmatically because they weren't interacted with.

So my change is correct - only remove the `cb.checked` setting from `toggleTodo`, NOT from the toggle-all handler.

Let me now verify the fix works by running the existing verification suite.

